Subject: GBA rollback: preserve VRAM contention latch and SIO event queues
Series-Step: 11/19 (mgba_dual 1.6-os4)
Origin: hanbang (this project)
요약: 되감기 정확성: VRAM 경합 마스크(stallMask)를 상태에 저장하고, 같은 시각 SIO 이벤트 순서와 빈 목록 끝을 정리.

The latched VRAM contention mask (previously a reserved word, flag bit 2 of the video flags) is saved and restored,
so a state taken in the middle of a scanline replays identically. Two SIO events with the same deadline keep their
original order on restore, and the queued and free node lists of the lockstep driver are rebuilt as disjoint terminated
lists. _calculateStallMask no longer needs the GBA struct (it takes DISPCNT and the BGCNT array).

---
diff --git a/include/mgba/internal/gba/serialize.h b/include/mgba/internal/gba/serialize.h
index bffc0caa6a7a..80c5521df6a4 100644
--- a/include/mgba/internal/gba/serialize.h
+++ b/include/mgba/internal/gba/serialize.h
@@ -112,9 +112,11 @@ mLOG_DECLARE_CATEGORY(GBA_STATE);
  *   | bits 8 - 31: Reserved
  * | 0x001E8 - 0x001EF: Reserved
  * 0x001F0 - 0x001FF: Video miscellaneous state
- * | 0x001F0 - 0x001F3: Reserved
+ * | 0x001F0 - 0x001F3: Latched VRAM contention mask (when flag bit 2 is set)
  * | 0x001F4 - 0x001F7: Next event
  * | 0x001F8 - 0x001FB: Miscellaneous flags
+ *   | bits 0 - 1: Video event mode
+ *   | bit 2: Latched VRAM contention mask is present
  * | 0x001FC - 0x001FF: Frame counter
  * 0x00200 - 0x00213: Timer 0
  * | 0x00200 - 0x00201: Reload value
@@ -288,6 +290,7 @@ DECL_BITS(GBASerializedAudioFlags2, ChBSource, 6, 2);
 
 DECL_BITFIELD(GBASerializedVideoFlags, uint32_t);
 DECL_BITS(GBASerializedVideoFlags, Mode, 0, 2);
+DECL_BIT(GBASerializedVideoFlags, StallMaskSaved, 2);
 
 DECL_BITFIELD(GBASerializedHWFlags1, uint16_t);
 DECL_BIT(GBASerializedHWFlags1, ReadWrite, 0);
@@ -369,7 +372,7 @@ struct GBASerializedState {
 	} audio;
 
 	struct {
-		int32_t reserved;
+		uint32_t stallMask;
 		int32_t nextEvent;
 		GBASerializedVideoFlags flags;
 		uint32_t frameCounter;
